# =========================================
# HelpDesk Pro - Environment Configuration
# =========================================
#
# The only runtime environment variables are the Firebase web app config,
# used by the frontend (apps/web) - see apps/web/.env.example for the full
# list and setup instructions. Copy that file to apps/web/.env.local.
#
# There is no backend server or database connection string to configure:
# the app talks to Firebase Authentication, Firestore, and Storage
# directly from the browser, with firebase/firestore.rules and
# firebase/storage.rules enforcing access control.
#
# Seeding demo data locally additionally requires a Firebase service
# account key (Project settings -> Service accounts -> Generate new
# private key) passed as an argument to `npm run seed:firebase` - never
# committed, never stored in an env file.
